// Title: HackTool - XORDump Execution
// Sigma ID: 66e563f9-1cbd-4a22-a957-d8b7c0f44372
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-01-28 | Modified: 2023-02-08
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036, T1003.001, credential-access
// Description: Detects suspicious use of XORDump process memory dumping utility
// False positives:
//   - Another tool that uses the command line switches of XORdump
// References:
//   - https://github.com/audibleblink/xordump
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_xordump.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\xordump.exe" or (ProcessCommandLine contains " -process lsass.exe " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -m comsvcs " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -m dbghelp " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -m dbgcore ")
